erate and specify the edit that stamps `result[\"sidecar_emitted\"]` on the completion path (e.g. in `record_completion_verdict` / `_emit_completion_sidecar` from emit()'s bool), or move the `sidecar_emitted` stamping into `completion_sidecar.emit()` itself, so the daemon record actually carries it.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["plan_review/__init__.py:578 `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"] = sidecar.emit(...)` — the CALLER stamps sidecar_emitted, not emit()","transition_close.py:188-189/198-199 `sidecar_written = completion_sidecar.emit(result, ...)` then returns `_outcome(...)`; result['sidecar_emitted'] is never set","_mcp_llm.py:129-130 `_plan_review_sidecar_fields`/`_gate_sidecar_fields` reads `sidecar_emitted` off `result` — absent for completion","ABSENCE: Design's three edits (emit stamps sidecar_reviewed_at; _mcp_llm guard widening; gate_runs parameterization) never set result['sidecar_emitted'] for completion"],"finding":"The AC 'The completion index record carries `sidecar_emitted` after a terminal run' requires an edit not described in the Design and not made to any named artifact. In the plan-review path, `sidecar_emitted` is stamped onto the verdict by the CALLER (plan_review/__init__.py:578 `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"] = sidecar.emit(...)`), NOT inside `emit()`. The plan's `emit()` change stamps only `sidecar_reviewed_at`. The completion daemon reaches `emit` via `_verify_completion_body -> _record_verify_completion -> record_completion_verdict -> emit`; `record_completion_verdict` (transition_close.py:189) captures emit's bool into a local `sidecar_written` and returns a separate `_outcome` dict, never writing `result[\"sidecar_emitted\"]`. Since `_gate_sidecar_fields` reads `sidecar_emitted` off `result`, the field will be absent and the AC (and the downstream `sidecar-not-emitted` reason branch it feeds) is unreachable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5bab96ed0f2fe49a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (completion_sidecar.py bullet); AC 'The completion index record carries sidecar_emitted after a terminal run'","norm_id":"nd1443511be014537","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A terminal async verify_completion run whose index record is inspected for sidecar_emitted","A completion FAIL where emit() failed: gate_runs' `sidecar-not-emitted` reason branch depends on rec['sidecar_emitted'] being False, which never lands"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:record_completion_verdict`, after `sidecar_written = completion_sidecar.emit(result, ...)`, add `result[\"sidecar_emitted\"] = sidecar_written` (mirroring plan_review/__init__.py:578), and list transition_close.py as a fourth touched artifact.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the completion emit path to stamp result['sidecar_emitted'] (mirroring plan_review/__init__.py:578) so _gate_sidecar_fields can forward it and the 'index record carries sidecar_emitted' AC is achievable, OR drop that AC and the sidecar_emitted-based reason branches for completion and justify the omission.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'The body already reads only sidecar_emitted / sidecar_reviewed_at, so no other change.'","search: 'sidecar_emitted' is written only in plan_review/{__init__.py:578,reuse.py,claimability.py,orchestrator.py}; no completion writer exists","transition_close.py:199 records sidecar_written inside result['record'], not result['sidecar_emitted']","AC line: '- [ ] The completion index record carries sidecar_emitted after a terminal run.'"],"finding":"The Design claims _gate_sidecar_fields needs 'no other change' because 'the body already reads only sidecar_emitted / sidecar_reviewed_at', but nothing on the completion path ever sets result['sidecar_emitted']; only the plan-review verdict is stamped with it (plan_review/__init__.py:578). The completion emit (record_completion_verdict -> completion_sidecar.emit) records only result['record']['sidecar_written'], so for every completion run sidecar_emitted is absent and the index record cannot carry it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f83a6e1361ebf2fca","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (_mcp_llm.py bullet) and AC 'The completion index record carries sidecar_emitted after a terminal run'","norm_id":"ne766afb5fc8b9f36","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Terminal async verify_completion job: _gate_sidecar_fields finds no sidecar_emitted key -> index record omits it -> the sidecar_emitted AC fails; the _review_result_status 'sidecar-not-emitted' branch (gate_runs.py:228) can never fire for completion because sidecar_emitted is never False, only absent."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have record_completion_verdict (or completion_sidecar.emit's caller) set result['sidecar_emitted'] = <emit bool> alongside the existing sidecar_written recording, so the terminal completion index record carries sidecar_emitted the same way plan-review does.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the COMPLETION_VERDICT timestamp source that the parameterised `_latest_review_result_timestamp` delegates to (e.g. add a `latest_completion_verdict_timestamp` reader in completion_sidecar mirroring plan_review.sidecar.latest_review_timestamp), since the existing latest_fail_verdict/latest_pass_record return verdict dicts, not int timestamps.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.432,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Parameterise `_latest_review_result_timestamp` and `_has_review_result_timestamp` by sidecar kind plus accepted schema set'","gate_runs.py:154-158 `_latest_review_result_timestamp` calls `sidecar.latest_review_timestamp(ticket_id, .